course: dictionary
lesson: 12612
title: Discreetly: doing things quietly and privately
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Discreetly is an adverb, a word that tells you how something is done. It means carefully and quietly, so that other people do not notice, or so that nobody is embarrassed. «Ben discreetly passed Sam a note under the desk.» Ben did not shout or wave the note around. He kept it quiet so the teacher would not see.
explain: The second meaning is about secrets. When you do something discreetly, you keep a private matter private. «Mum discreetly told me my zip was open.» Mum did not call across the playground. She spared me from being embarrassed in front of my friends.
explain: Look at the words around discreetly to check its meaning. Quietly, carefully and private are clues. Then swap in your meaning: «Mum quietly and privately told me my zip was open» still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: Discreetly is an adverb, so it tells you how an action happens.
fact: «Discreetly» means carefully and quietly, so that other people do not notice.
fact: «Discreetly» can also mean in a way that keeps a secret or private matter private.
fact: Discreet is the adjective, and discreetly is the adverb made from it.
fact: Discreetly is often used with actions such as «discreetly left the room» or «discreetly mentioned».
exercise: «Ben discreetly passed Sam a note under the desk.» What does discreetly mean? | Very fast | Angrily | *Carefully and quietly, so others did not notice | Loudly, so everyone could see
exercise: «Mum discreetly told me my zip was open.» Why did Mum do it discreetly? | *To keep it private and spare me embarrassment | To shout across the room | To make everyone laugh | Because she was angry with me
exercise: «The waiter discreetly placed the bill on the table.» Find and copy the adverb. | placed | waiter | *discreetly | table
test: «She discreetly left the room.» What does discreetly suggest? | *She went out quietly, so no one made a fuss | She shouted goodbye to everyone | She was crying and sad | She danced out of the room
test: Jo asks her friend to keep her secret. She says, «I'll be discreet.» What does discreetly mean in «keep a secret discreetly»? | Telling everyone the news | Writing it on the board | *Keeping the private matter private | Forgetting it straight away
exam: «The teacher discreetly mentioned the mistake to me alone.» What does discreetly mean here? | Slowly, for a very long time | Loudly, in front of the whole class | *In a private, careful way, so I would not be embarrassed | Angrily, with a red face
